    "body": "Closing a window next to a group of windows can enlarge a `winfixwidth` or `winfixheight` window even when an unfixed window can take the freed space. In the reported layout, a 30-column fixed window grows to 51 columns; with this change it stays at 30 and its unfixed neighbour receives the space.\n\nRespect fixed sizes while resizing the receiving frame, with a fallback when fixed windows prevent it from filling the space. Use the same policy to restore the layout after a failed window move. This follows the existing screen-resize strategy.\n\nThe documented fixed-size behaviour applies with `equalalways` enabled. The reported case also reproduces in Vim 9.2.1150; this is a shared behaviour change, not a Neovim regression.\n\nValidation on macOS:\n- Width and height regressions fail on master `402a494f47` and pass with the fix.\n- Eight cases cover both directions, fixed and unfixed windows, all-fixed fallback, failed-move restoration, and subsequent screen resizing. The restoration checks also fail if only the removal path is changed.\n- All 17 window command tests and 144 window API tests pass.\n- C lint, StyLua, and `git diff --check` pass.\n\nFixes #42281.\n\nAI-assisted.\n",
